(Ord. No. 18-04, § 1, 4-24-2018)

755:
An application for a parade permit shall be filed with the city tax and license clerk, who shall promptly convey the application to the chief of police or his designee, time being of the essence. Such application shall be on form(s) provided by the city and shall be filed not less than five calendar days prior to the proposed parade, assembly or demonstration. The application shall contain the following information:
(1) The name(s), address(es), telephone number(s) and email address of the person or persons sponsoring, organizing, or conducting the event; the name and a cellular telephone number of the sponsor's contact person who will be continuously available by phone during the event and for 24 hours prior thereto;
(2) The date and time of the parade or event;
(3) The proposed route of the parade, including its assembly and disassembly points, if permission is sought to shorten the route or follow a different route from that set forth in section 78-68 of this article; the proposed location(s) for a protest or demonstration, and the written consent of any private property owner on whose property the event is to occur;
(4) Approximate number of participants, and type of vehicles, animals, marching units, bands, and floats to be involved, including any sound amplification to be used;
(5) Estimate of the number of persons or spectators who may observe the event;
(6) Estimate of the maximum length of the parade and/or time during which street intersections along the parade route may be obstructed;
(7) Estimate whether any opposition or contra-demonstration is anticipated and what security measures, if any, the sponsor or organizer has taken to provide security for participants;
(8) A description of any unusual problems anticipated concerning traffic or public safety, or a statement that no unusual problems are anticipated;
(9) Where a separate permit is required by the Georgia Department of Transportation to occupy or obstruct a state route or highway, such permit shall be issued by GDOT as a condition precedent to applying for a city permit.
(10) All applications shall be signed by the event sponsor or organizer, who shall swear before a notary that the information contained therein is true and correct. Any false statement in an application shall be grounds for denial or revocation of a permit and/or denial of future permits.
No fee or charge shall be imposed upon an applicant for a permit under this article.
(Ord. No. 18-04, § 1, 4-24-2018)

